1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,641
If you're chasing someone who doesn't want you, you're losing more than time.

2
00:00:04,091 --> 00:00:08,952
This morning I'm making breakfast. And boom. Flashbacks. Five months on dating apps.

3
00:00:09,403 --> 00:00:12,378
Five months I'm never getting back. Bro. Who was that guy?

4
00:00:13,478 --> 00:00:17,603
Here's the game nobody explains. Chase or get chased. That's it.

5
00:00:18,053 --> 00:00:23,304
You chase someone who doesn't want you. Someone chases you, and you don't want them. Everybody loses.

6
00:00:23,754 --> 00:00:27,094
And everybody's trying to prove something. Prove what? Nobody knows.

7
00:00:27,544 --> 00:00:32,677
"Hey, I'm worth looking at." Just [bleep] off. I don't even care if you exist.

8
00:00:33,128 --> 00:00:37,829
That should've been my mentality. Was it? No. Of course not. Stupid idiot.

9
00:00:38,929 --> 00:00:41,393
I didn't even want that person. Not even a little.

10
00:00:41,843 --> 00:00:46,050
One minute. That's all it would've taken. One minute of using my brain.

11
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:53,070
But they pull away, and suddenly I'm the one trying. Did I do something? Can I prove I'm better? Am I good enough?

12
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:56,052
Good enough for what? I didn't even like you.

13
00:00:57,152 --> 00:01:03,541
It's not them you want. It's the attention. You want to be wanted. That's the trap.

14
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:09,039
They act high value, so you assume they are. They might not be. Acting is free.

15
00:01:09,489 --> 00:01:14,365
And the more desperate you get, the further they go. Like a cat. Chase the cat, the cat leaves.

16
00:01:14,816 --> 00:01:21,121
It's Gojo's Infinity, and daddy Mahoraga isn't on your side. You get closer and closer. You never touch it.

17
00:01:22,221 --> 00:01:28,661
The funny part? I saw it happening. In real time. I looked at it, said "interesting," and kept going.

18
00:01:29,111 --> 00:01:29,819
It's like a drug.

19
00:01:30,269 --> 00:01:34,340
Meanwhile, my actual life is just sitting there. Hello? Remember me?

20
00:01:35,439 --> 00:01:39,798
I was obsessed with training. Obsessed. One word in my head. Perfection.

21
00:01:40,247 --> 00:01:44,043
I had goals so big I couldn't say them out loud. People would think I'm crazy.

22
00:01:44,493 --> 00:01:49,043
And what happened to them? Forgot them. Completely. For a situation on my phone.

23
00:01:49,493 --> 00:01:53,889
Now I'm training sad, thinking about one person, while making another person sad.

24
00:01:54,339 --> 00:01:57,588
How do you even manage that? Talent, honestly.

25
00:01:58,688 --> 00:02:02,480
So how did I fix it? Genius over here jumped into a new situationship.

26
00:02:02,930 --> 00:02:07,971
Beautiful. Amazing. Stupid. Everyone could see it except the guy doing it. Me.

27
00:02:09,070 --> 00:02:10,347
Then I got my wake-up call.

28
00:02:10,798 --> 00:02:13,574
I'd been chased before. Everybody has. But not like this.

29
00:02:14,025 --> 00:02:17,352
We'd known each other less than a week, and I was already her whole life.

30
00:02:17,801 --> 00:02:21,799
I don't answer for twenty minutes. I open my phone. Twenty messages.

31
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:26,080
Do you wanna go? Do you still wanna talk to me? Do I even matter to you?

32
00:02:26,530 --> 00:02:30,806
It's been a week. One week. And your whole life already revolves around me?

33
00:02:31,256 --> 00:02:34,104
And then it hit me. Wait. Do I act like this?

34
00:02:34,554 --> 00:02:39,842
Not that bad. Maybe five percent. But even one percent, I'm not accepting that from myself.

35
00:02:40,942 --> 00:02:45,655
Hold on. My neighbor is staring at me through his window. What the heck. Anyway.

36
00:02:46,754 --> 00:02:51,256
I'm not saying I'm better than her. Everybody is better than this. Even her.

37
00:02:51,705 --> 00:02:57,598
We're all just fooled. Movies and social media sell us the drama. We think we want it. We don't.

38
00:02:58,048 --> 00:03:04,929
And these apps? Use your head. They don't want you to leave. They want your money. You stay stuck, they stay happy.

39
00:03:06,029 --> 00:03:08,146
So leave. And don't tell me you're "resisting."

40
00:03:08,596 --> 00:03:13,982
If a knife is cutting you, you don't resist the knife. You stay away from it. That's it. Let it heal.

41
00:03:14,432 --> 00:03:18,906
But we keep going back. Maybe this time the knife is different. It's not.

42
00:03:20,006 --> 00:03:21,919
Put the phone down. Don't eat slop.

43
00:03:22,370 --> 00:03:28,212
And if I catch you at McDonald's, I hope God strikes you with thunder. Do you know how many ingredients are in that thing?

44
00:03:28,663 --> 00:03:31,814
Go outside. Look around. Go back to the old ways.

45
00:03:32,265 --> 00:03:36,536
Yeah, it's not that easy anymore. Doesn't matter. Find a way.

46
00:03:37,636 --> 00:03:42,980
Remember being a kid? Everything was bright. You enjoyed everything. That's your natural state.

47
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:45,820
You can go back. Give it a month. Maybe two.

48
00:03:46,270 --> 00:03:52,935
"My life is ruined." Relax. Remember that high school relationship? The one that was forever? Yeah.

49
00:03:53,385 --> 00:03:56,152
You survived. And if you're in high school right now, you will too.

50
00:03:57,252 --> 00:04:02,116
You can be reborn. For real. People change their whole lives. You're not stuck being the same person forever.

51
00:04:02,566 --> 00:04:07,026
You're human. Humans make mistakes. It wouldn't be fair if you only got one shot.

52
00:04:07,476 --> 00:04:10,850
I believe that's from God. Whatever you believe, that's up to you.

53
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:20,168
I'm not saying don't chase love. Chase a healthy one. A loving wife. A loving husband. Hardworking. Respectful. Grinding for each other. Kids.

54
00:04:20,618 --> 00:04:22,187
Not whatever that was on the app.

55
00:04:23,287 --> 00:04:27,636
Honestly, this video was never supposed to be about dating apps. [bleep] the dating apps.

56
00:04:28,086 --> 00:04:33,963
We sit there going, this piece of crap looks good. No, this piece of crap is bad. It's all crap.

57
00:04:35,064 --> 00:04:39,170
I'm talking about being alive. We say "get a life" like it means "get a job."

58
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:43,757
People go crazy over gold. What the [bleep] is gold? It's a metal.

59
00:04:44,206 --> 00:04:50,620
But being alive? Memories. Feelings. A character you get to build. And that time isn't coming back.

60
00:04:51,069 --> 00:04:54,985
You could be doing anything with it. And you're checking if somebody texted back.

61
00:04:55,435 --> 00:05:01,935
Don't waste it, man. Enjoy it. So one day you look back and ask, who was that guy? And you're proud of him.

62
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:06,587
Don't do anything illegal today. Love you all equally. Bye.
